# `make run-gui` as a person runs it (`make test-hand-run`): the image
# $(KERNEL), the disk tools/run-disk.sh keeps, and the same QEMU command line
# (RUN_GUI_CMD, --net included), with no window (`--display-opts none`) and a QMP socket to
# read the screen and type (the runner's GUI script, tools/test-runner/src/gui.rs).
# The desktop's terminal has a shell with its volume: the prompt is the home.
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
serial compd:
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type echo ready\r
screen ready
screen ~> _
# `make run-gui` has the network by default (--net): the terminal's shell has
# the root connection, the lease is in, and the gateway answers an echo.
pause 3000
type net status\r
prefix net0  up  52:54:00:12:34:56
type ping -c 1 10.0.2.2\r
prefix 1 sent, 1 received, 0% loss
screen ~> _
type poweroff\r
exit
